Package: PrecFact
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Precision Factor Analysis for Gaussian Graphical Models
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Noirrit Kiran", "Chandra", email = "noirritchandra@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cph"), comment = "author of the original PrecFact code"),
    person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", email = "bhadury@upenn.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = "portable package, post-processing and figures"),
    person("Josef", "Leydold", role = "ctb", comment = "GIG generator adapted from GIGrvg"),
    person("Wolfgang", "Hormann", role = "ctb", comment = "GIG generator adapted from GIGrvg"))
Description: Estimates a high-dimensional Gaussian precision matrix and its
    conditional independence graph with the precision factor model of Chandra,
    Mueller and Sarkar (2026) <doi:10.1214/24-BA1461>. The precision matrix is
    decomposed into a low-rank and a diagonal part, Omega = Lambda Lambda' + Delta,
    with a Dirichlet-Laplace prior on the loadings and a Dirichlet process prior on
    the diagonal. A latent variable representation of the decomposition yields a
    Gibbs sampler that scales to thousands of variables, and edges are selected by
    controlling the posterior false discovery rate. Includes network and heat map
    figures, edge and hub tables, and a simulator.
